<title>DUBAI: Commercial Bank of Dubai ups net, in bonus issue.</title>
<headline>Commercial Bank of Dubai ups net, in bonus issue.</headline>
<dateline>DUBAI 1997-02-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Year to December 31, 1996</p>
<p>		    (million dirhams unless stated)</p>
<p> Net income				    143.83     vs     121.58</p>
<p> Profit available for appropriation    145.45     vs     124.27</p>
<p> Net interest income			 169.03     vs     136.05</p>
<p> Other income				   52.28     vs	53.08</p>
<p> Provisions, other expenses		 15.05     vs	14.16</p>
<p> Total proposed cash dividend	     46.20     vs	61.60</p>
<p> Proposed bonus issue			 30.80     vs	nil</p>
<p> Assets					3,907.12     vs   3,319.82</p>
<p>Full Name: Commercial Bank of Dubai psc</p>
<p>Note - The Dubai government owns 20 percent of the bank. The rest is held by UAE nationals. In 1996 there were 30.8 million shares in issue. The board has recommended a bonus issue of 3.08 million shares.</p>
<p>During the year the bank obtained a licence to operate an offshore banking unit in the Cayman Islands, which is scheduled to start operations this year.</p>
</text>
